      "content": "Definition: Understandability refers to how easily developers can comprehend and maintain the test code.\n\nTask: Improve the understandability of the test `NullInputStream_ESTest_test14.java` (path:- /Users/tenghaha/Projects/New_Agent_understandability_improvement/data/original/commons-io/auto/testcases/NullInputStream_ESTest/NullInputStream_ESTest_test14.java). The refactored code must be syntactically correct and compilable against the provided CUT signatures. Do not alter the runtime behaviour of the original test: the same methods must be called with the same arguments and produce the same expected outcomes.\n"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the test. It verifies two things:\n1. `available()` is capped at `Integer.MAX_VALUE` when the stream size exceeds it (size `2147485141L` > `Integer.MAX_VALUE`)\n2. Mark is supported by default\n\nLet me write the improved version with better variable names and a named constant for the magic number.Now let me compile-check the test.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored test replaces the magic number `2147485141L` with a named constant `SIZE_EXCEEDING_INT_MAX` and uses descriptive variable names (`stream`, `availableBytes`) instead of the auto-generated `nullInputStream0` and `int0`, making the intent of the test immediately clear."
    }
  ],
  "last_code": "package org.apache.commons.io.input;\n\nimport org.junit.Test;\nimport static org.junit.Assert.*;\nimport static org.evosuite.runtime.EvoAssertions.*;\nimport java.io.EOFException;\nimport java.io.IOException;\nimport org.evosuite.runtime.EvoRunner;\nimport org.evosuite.runtime.EvoRunnerParameters;\nimport org.junit.runner.RunWith;\n\n@RunWith(EvoRunner.class)\n@EvoRunnerParameters(mockJVMNonDeterminism = true, useVFS = true, useVNET = true, resetStaticState = true, separateClassLoader = false)\npublic class NullInputStream_ESTest_test14 extends NullInputStream_ESTest_scaffolding {\n\n    // Stream size exceeds Integer.MAX_VALUE to verify available() caps its return value at Integer.MAX_VALUE\n    private static final long SIZE_EXCEEDING_INT_MAX = 2147485141L;\n\n    @Test(timeout = 4000)\n    public void test14() throws Throwable {\n        NullInputStream stream = new NullInputStream(SIZE_EXCEEDING_INT_MAX);\n\n        int availableBytes = stream.available();\n\n        assertEquals(Integer.MAX_VALUE, availableBytes);\n        assertTrue(stream.markSupported());\n    }\n}\n",
